      10 ## Authentication Flow
      11
      12 ADS has a **two-tier authentication system**:
      13
      14 ### 1. Classic ADS Backend (External)
      15 - **Source**: `/adsabs/core/classic/user.py`
      16 - Makes HTTP requests to `ADS_LOGIN_URL` configured in `config.ADS_LOGIN_URL`
      17 - Functions:
      18   - `get_classic_user(login, password)` — validates credentials against classic ADS
      19   - `create_classic_user()`, `update_classic_password()`, `reset_classic_password()`
      20   - Returns JSON with fields: `cookie`, `loggedin`, `myadsid`, `fullname`, `email`, `openurl_icon`
      21
      22 ### 2. Local MongoDB User Records
      23 - **Model**: `AdsUserRecord` in `/adsabs/modules/user/models.py`
      24 - Stored in MongoDB collection `ads_users`
      25 - Key fields:
      26   - `cookie_id` — unique identifier from classic ADS (index)
      27   - `username` — email address (unique index)
      28   - `anonymous` (bool) — marks if user is anonymous
      29   - `active` (bool) — account active status
      30   - `developer_key` — API developer key (if enabled)
      31   - `developer_perms` — dict of API permissions
      32   - `remote_login_system` — login provider URL
      33   - `myads_id` — link to classic ADS
      34
      35 ## Anonymous vs Authenticated Users
      36
      37 **Anonymous users:**
      38 - `anonymous=True` in user record
      39 - Don't have a real login
      40 - Generated UUID stored in cookie `config.COOKIE_ADSABS2_NAME`
      41 - Used for tracking unlogged visitors
      42 - See: `/adsabs/core/before_request_funcs.py:set_user_cookie_id()`
      43
      44 **Authenticated users:**
      45 - `anonymous=False`, `active=True`
      46 - Have valid credentials in classic ADS
      47 - Created via `AdsUser.from_classic_user()` which syncs data from classic ADS
      48 - Updates username, name, myads_id from classic ADS on each login
      49
      50 ## User Object Hierarchy
      51 ```
      52 AdsUser (base class)
      53 ├── is_authenticated() → returns AUTHENTICATED=True
      54 ├── is_active() → checks user_rec.active
      55 ├── is_anonymous() → checks user_rec.anonymous
      56 └── AdsApiUser (extends AdsUser for API access)
      57     └── adds developer_key, developer_perms, permission checking
      58 ```
      59
      60 ## Key Flows
      61
      62 **New user first-time login:**
      63 1. Credentials sent to classic ADS via `get_classic_user()`
      64 2. Classic ADS returns cookie_id + user metadata
      65 3. `AdsUser.from_classic_user()` creates/updates local MongoDB record
      66 4. User logged in via Flask-Login
      67
      68 **Session Management:**
      69 - Flask-Login loads user via `load_user(id)` in app.py:123 → calls `AdsUser.from_id(cookie_id)`
      70 - Looks up user record in MongoDB by cookie_id

