      10 ## Permission System
      11
      12 **NOT traditional rate limiting** (no requests-per-minute). Instead: **capability-based access control**.
      13
      14 ### Three Permission Levels
      15 Defined in `/adsabs/modules/api/api_user.py:26-52`:
      16
      17 **1. Basic** (default)
      18 - `max_rows`: 100 results per query
      19 - `max_start`: 10,000 (can't paginate past 10k)
      20 - `facets`: disabled
      21 - `highlight`: disabled
      22 - Used for anonymous/free users
      23
      24 **2. Devel** (development)
      25 - `max_rows`: 200
      26 - `max_start`: 50,000
      27 - `facets`: enabled
      28 - `facet_limit_max`: 100 (limit per facet)
      29 - `highlight`: enabled
      30 - `highlight_limit_max`: 4
      31 - `highlight_fields`: selected fields from config
      32
      33 **3. Collab** (collaboration/power users)
      34 - `max_rows`: 200
      35 - `max_start`: None (no pagination limit)
      36 - `allowed_fields`: extended field list from config
      37 - `facet_limit_max`: 500
      38 - `highlight`: enabled, all fields allowed
      39
      40 ### API Authentication
      41
      42 **Developer Key Flow** (in `/adsabs/modules/api/views.py`):
      43 1. Client passes `dev_key` query parameter
      44 2. `@api_user_required` decorator validates the key
      45 3. Looks up user via `AdsApiUser.from_dev_key(dev_key)` — queries MongoDB `developer_key` field
      46 4. Caches result 60 seconds with `@cache.memoize(60)`
      47 5. Returns 403 if dev_key invalid or unrecognized
      48
      49 **Dev Key Security:**
      50 - Generated as random 16-char alphanumeric via `_create_dev_key()`
      51 - Stored as SHA512 hash with salt in `developer_perms['developer_key']`
      52 - Validation uses `validate_dev_key(dev_key, hash_struct)` — constant-time comparison
      53 - See lines 60-89 in api_user.py for hashing strategy
      54
      55 ### IP Whitelisting
      56
      57 Each user can set `allowed_ips` in their `developer_perms`:
      58 - `get_allowed_ips()` — returns list of IP addresses/CIDR ranges
      59 - `ip_allowed(request_ip)` — checks if request IP matches any whitelisted range
      60 - Uses Python `ipaddress` module for CIDR parsing
      61 - Returns `True` if no IPs configured (no restriction)
      62 - Applied via `@api_ip_allowed` decorator in views.py
      63
      64 ### Permission Enforcement
      65
      66 In `check_permissions()` (line 174):
      67 - Validates each request against user's `developer_perms`
      68 - Checks:
      69   - Facets are enabled + within limit
      70   - Row count doesn't exceed `max_rows`
      71   - Pagination `start` doesn't exceed `max_start`
      72   - Requested fields in allowed set
      73   - Highlight fields enabled + within limit
      74
      75 Raises `ApiPermissionError` if any check fails.
      76
      77 ### API Endpoints Requiring Authentication
      78 All endpoints in `/adsabs/modules/api/views.py` require:
      79 1. `@api_user_required` — valid dev_key
      80 2. `@api_ip_allowed` — whitelisted IP (if configured)
      81
      82 Endpoints:
      83 - `/api/settings/` — returns user's permissions
      84 - `/api/search/` — search with permissions
      85 - `/api/search/metrics/` — search + citation metrics
      86 - `/api/record/<id>/` — single record lookup
      87 - `/api/record/<id>/metrics/` — record + metrics
      88
      89 ### Monitoring
      90 All API calls logged to statsd:
      91 - `api.user.authentication.success/failed/unknown`
      92 - `api.user.access_from_ip.denied`
      93 - `api.search.success/invalid`
      94 - `api.record.success/not_found`

